    "section_evoo_v3_faq_rRJhLR": {
      "type": "section-evoo-v3-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_BFc6Am": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does \"scientifically balanced\" mean for this formula?",
            "answer": "<p>It means each mineral was selected for its specific biological role and for how it works with the others. Copper and Zinc share Cu/Zn superoxide dismutase as a cofactor — the same antioxidant enzyme. Copper also prevents the copper depletion that sustained zinc use can cause. Selenium activates antioxidant glutathione peroxidase enzymes and thyroid hormone conversion deiodinases — two functions in one mineral. Manganese covers MnSOD — the mitochondrial antioxidant the other four minerals can't activate. The formula is balanced because the five minerals fill each other's gaps.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_pgG9dR": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why does this say it \"contributes to normal immune function\" rather than \"boosts immunity\"?",
            "answer": "<p>Under FSSAI regulations, health supplements can only make structure/function claims — statements about how a nutrient contributes to normal physiological processes. \"Contributes to the normal function of the immune system\" is the evidence-based, FSSAI-compliant way to state what Copper, Zinc, and Selenium are documented to do. Claims like \"boosts immunity\" are not permitted under Indian nutraceutical regulations for this product category.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_zet6LP": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why are four minerals at 100% RDA and Zinc at 83.33%?",
            "answer": "<p>The 11 mg of elemental Zinc per tablet (83.33% RDA) was deliberately calibrated — it delivers meaningful daily zinc supplementation while staying well below the upper tolerable intake limit. More importantly, excessive zinc over time can deplete copper. By including Copper at 1.7 mg (100% RDA) in the same tablet and keeping zinc at 83.33% rather than 100%, the formula maintains mineral balance rather than creating an imbalance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Q6TUxh": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "The label says it contains Lactose Monohydrate — does this mean it's not suitable for me?",
            "answer": "<p>If you have diagnosed lactose intolerance or a milk protein allergy, consult your physician before taking AIMINERAL. Lactose Monohydrate is used as a pharmaceutical-grade tablet binder and is present at excipient-level amounts — but individuals with significant dairy sensitivities should check with their doctor. The product is also not suitable for strict vegans due to this excipient.</p>"
